WEBVTT

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.440
You sure make a flashy show
of it as always, Ayano.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.230
You were facing a D-Class, right?

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:56.360
I can't go easy with my work
and cause damage to civilians, can I?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.280
But are they really civilians?

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:03.160
Anyway, can I rely on you to silence them?

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.170
Can you say it's a gag order
at the least?

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.130
Oh, hold on a sec!

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.340
Can we go now?

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.470
Oh... Yes.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.140
Nooooo!

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:24.980
Tony!

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.980
Tony!

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.740
EPISODE 4
UNOBTAINABLE LINGERING

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.660
Sorry to make you wait.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.620
You owe me a bottle of wine.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.580
We can take our time to drink today, right?

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.670
I'm sorry.
This case is a race against time.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:20.420
Didn't you say the same thing when you called me
out last week to start an auction immediately?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.470
The chief of Metropolitan Police
came storming in afterwards.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.680
He told me to stop
making unnecessary interferences.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.430
Sorry to trouble you all the time!

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.810
This one is on me, okay?

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:40.860
We twisted so many arms, but in the end
couldn't retrieve the core, either.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.620
Because of that, we've planned
power outages again today!

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.450
Jeez, it's such a pain in the butt
to coordinate this!

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.170
We finally got money,
but the electricity isn't turning back on.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:59.420
Thanks to us, the peace of the city
was upheld, too. Huh?

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.140
#anothercandlepartytonight

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.140
Whaaaaat?

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.970
You want me to bow down
to the chief again?

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.020
Please, Linfa!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:14.350
You're the only one I can rely on!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:18.480
Or rather, if I ask you,
most things aren't impossible.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.150
But he's a real pain to deal with!

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:25.530
He's the type that isn't satisfied
unless everything's under his control.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.450
All the more reason!

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.250
It helps us a lot that the chief
of Metropolitan Police knows about this.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.660
But if you ask one favor after another,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.750
who knows what kind of unreasonable
demands he'll come up with later?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.260
You drank quite a bit
with my money, didn't you?

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.260
If I can order one more bottle,
I might consider it.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.230
I'm counting on you, okay?

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:57.860
Fine, all right.
I'll talk it out with the police.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.070
I'll wait for your call.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.440
See you.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.410
Oh, by the way...

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:07.910
Huh?

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:07.910
is he doing well?

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.660
That younger ex-boyfriend of yours.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.710
You still see him on your job
if I recall correctly.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:18.290
Can it be that this favor you're asking now
has something to do with him?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.880
Why do you remember
trivial things like that?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:26.050
Of course, after hearing you fawn over him,
gripe about him and cry over him all the time...

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.550
I was really surprised
when I heard about it for the first time.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.890
That righteous little Ayano
actually turned out to like young guys.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.560
Don't say such scandalous things!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:40.900
I mean, you broke up
because he became an adult, right?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.990
What do you think your best friend is?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.700
Hold on! Wait up!

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.820
Linfa!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.630
Shu!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.710
Sorry, I'll be right over.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.970
What do you want to do for dinner?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.470
There's another planned power outage tonight.
Should we eat out for the first time in a while?

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:14.220
We got paid, so let's go
for a luxurious dinner!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.480
Let's add eggs to beef bowls!
And large bowls are okay, too!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:23.730
I'm sorry, but the first half and second half
of that statement don't connect.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.030
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.160
Hello, Kisara!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:36.000
You're glistening like an evening primrose
that quietly blooms in the shade!

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:41.250
So did the first half and second half
of that statement connect?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.000
Why are you here?

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:47.760
Well, I heard that this district where you live
is still out of power this morning,

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.720
so I couldn't help myself!

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.090
By the way, who is this?

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.010
Are you all right?
Are you troubled by anything?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.640
Is it bothering you?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:53.510
Yeah.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.600
Especially this all too unique personality.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:57.640
I can help you out at any time!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.640
Right.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.350
Oh, you must be the one!

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.770
The one that takes advantage of Kisara's kindness,
good nature and ability to take care of others,

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:07.440
and makes meals out of her.
A demon of an abusive boyfriend!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:14.200
Well, I do make my meals with her, but we're
under a mutual contract. I mean, consent.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.450
So yeah, I do make my meals with her!

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:20.290
Such a vague affirmation
makes it difficult to denounce you!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.040
Huh? So what's the meaning of all this?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.210
What are you going to do with Kisara?

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.840
That aside, who were you again?

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.380
Now, I'll have you answer me!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.380
Are you one of Kisara's classmates?

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:32.550
HACHISUKA ACADEMY
STUDENT COUNCIL
PRESIDENT
MIKHAIL HACHISUKA

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.550
This is who I am!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.550
Oh...

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.800
Thanks for the courteous introduction.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:48.690
This place...

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:53.570
Oh!

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:57.950
That aside, there's some good material here!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:03.420
So, as the grandson of the first mayor
Yoshiteru Hachisuka,

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.420
and the first son of the current mayor
Masataka Hachisuka,

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.550
I, Mikhail Hachisuka,
will declare this to you!

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.880
A rootless vagabond, a penniless man
with no future prospects,

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:19.520
a freeloader that lives each day sponging money
from women is not suitable for Kisara!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:24.480
Now, gather up your belongings
and get out of this city!

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.820
My Bayron City does not welcome you!

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.730
If you don't even have
the money to move out,

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:33.110
I'll show compassion and provide you
with the moving costs—

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.110
Ayano heading to a love hotel with a guy

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.660
So, what exactly is the meaning of this?

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:41.580
H-Huh?

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.250
Wh-What's the meaning of this, really?

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.540
I didn't think you'd actually show up.
I see you still haven't gotten over him yet.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.880
And you don't need to do such petty things!

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.800
I'm Assistant Inspector Mikami of Bayron City
Special Criminal Operations Prevention Bureau,

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.470
also known as...

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:01.470
the Anti-Demon Bureau.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:02.930
A detective...

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.390
From the Anti-Demon Bureau, even.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.690
Regarding the suspect apprehended
at last night's Demon Hazard...

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.740
his name is Tony Rossi,
a member of the crime syndicate Orcas.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:19.580
Isn't that the mafia that took root
in the Italian resident district of Downtown?

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:25.210
Yes. For a conflict against Serpiente
the Latin American crime syndicate,

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.210
they seem to have borrowed
the powers of a demon.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.540
Can't they at least stay human for fights?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.090
We received information...

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:38.300
from Miss Yugiri here that she saw Tony Rossi
a few days ago here at this park.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:45.060
This is where Shu went behind my back
to secretly meet up with Ayano a few days ago.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:49.020
That wasn't behind your back at all!
I'm terribly sorry!

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:52.730
By the way, this is Tony Rossi.
Do you recognize him?

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:54.940
This guy, on that day...

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.120
So, along with Miss Yugiri the witness,

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.790
I'm tracing the footsteps of the man
who'd been seen with Tony Rossi.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:09.960
It's not for stoking foolish passion or for a
struggle between unfaithful and faithful love,

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:15.130
or for bloodshed stemming
from jealousy, so please rest assured.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.760
Oh, that's enough of that!

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.760
In other words, that guy...

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.850
Yes.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:25.430
The guy pretending to be a salesman for a pyramid
scheme, guiding people to contracts with demons.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:28.770
The chances are high
that he's such a mastermind.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:32.520
Got that? You seem to have
some weird misunderstanding.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.530
- In the first place, we—
- Why...

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.780
Huh?

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.780
Why are you investigating all this
without saying a word to me?

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:46.790
You knew I've been chasing after the demon
that killed my family for years now.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.040
Oh, that's because...

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.630
Is he the possessive type?

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.170
Shut up.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.880
Yes, Mikami here.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.260
Yes.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.880
We're after the tracks
of the suspect right now.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.800
Yes, yes.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.010
What?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.260
Tony Rossi has been murdered?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:17.280
And did he say anything before he died?

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.570
No. It seems he was killed
before he regained consciousness.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.030
Is this a silencing
involving demons, you think?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.490
No, I don't think we can follow
that line of investigation.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.540
This is the weapon.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.920
See this engraving of a snake on the hilt?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.380
This is the emblem
of the leaders of Serpiente.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.380
This is simply revenge from the mafia.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.880
They were brazen enough to show themselves
on the surveillance cameras, too.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:46.060
It looks like we'll have to interrogate
members of Serpiente, then.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:50.810
That means the investigation for the pyramid
scheme salesman will be paused for now.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:51.640
Um...

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.390
Huh?

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:56.820
A woman named Maria Tissi supposedly
is the victim's significant other.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.690
She's making a huge scene,
completely out of control.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.780
Yeah, okay.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:04.990
That again?

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.240
I was asked the same thing
just moments ago.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.000
What kind of person asked you?

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.250
A man with a green coat.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:17.040
His hair was ruffled,
and his eyes were lifeless. Oh!

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:19.800
He looked a bit younger than you.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.260
He's not that much younger than me!

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.760
Wasn't the investigation put on hold?

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.560
Well, even if we're told that,
neither of us can really stop doing this...

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.440
right?

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:35.860
Yoshito Kashima.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.940
The college student
who tried to assassinate the mayor.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:42.320
This has been bugging me ever since...

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.700
but now I remember thanks to listening
to the detective's story.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:49.660
About a week ago, we saw him right here.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:54.080
Right! He's the student who was totally
falling for that pyramid scheme, right?

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.330
I didn't think that was a temptation
from a demon though!

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.670
So is that pyramid scheme guy
the mastermind?

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.050
His living area totally overlaps with ours!

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.840
Maybe he actually lives close by?

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.550
So, where to next?

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.340
Are you going to go visit
that college student? Or—

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.220
You should go home!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.180
To begin with,
this is information that I obtained!

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:15.600
But it's more efficient
if we split up and work together!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.560
C'mon, let's help each other out here!

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.570
So what is it? Are you mad
that I was pouting earlier?

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.610
I'm sorry! I apologize!

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:28.490
So please, stop being angry, Ayano!

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.200
What's this apology for?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.870
No matter how much you've apologized,
you haven't once made a compromise!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.500
Huh?

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.630
You're always like that, Shu!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:41.710
No matter who's right and who's wrong,
you laugh like some fool!

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:46.130
And you never lend an ear
to any of my opinions or feelings! Not once!

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.260
A-Ayano?

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.180
You pretend to lose,
but you never back down!

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:53.520
You pretend to fawn on me, but you never
show me what's deep inside your heart!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:14:00.440
You never fully trust me or any human.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.110
You only trust her!

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.980
That demon!

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.240
It was the same thing back then, too.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.660
Back then?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:11.580
Your first birthday
after we started living together.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:16.620
I was preparing for a party at home
and waited deep into the night.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.330
But you never came home!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:23.300
And the next morning, I blamed you for things,
but you just kept kowtowing and apologizing!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:25.090
But actually,

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:28.800
you were chasing a Demonically Possessed that got away
because of my blunder all by yourself that day!

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.300
You didn't say one word
about that and kept apologizing!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.520
H-Huh? What?

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.180
Shu?

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.940
Y-Yeah. That's right.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.690
I was in the wrong. I'm sorry.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.900
You don't remember?

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.400
N-No! I-It's nothing like that!

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:52.950
A-Ayano—

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.790
Are you really okay by yourself?

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.210
They got their revenge...

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:09.550
so they'll hand over the one guy
who did the killing, and it's a done deal. I think.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.100
Come on now!

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.780
Why do things end up this way?

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.290
I won't forgive you
no matter how much you apologize!

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.290
That works out in my favor.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.880
Why are you angry?

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.300
Nothing, really.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.720
Is it because Shu had forgotten?

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:57.640
About that night and how you made an effort
to cook omurice and waited all night?

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.730
The fact that you were wearing sexy lingerie
you bought through mail order?

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:06.190
The fact that you were planning
to offer yourself as the birthday gift.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.400
That you were fully intent
on not letting him sleep that night.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:11.280
Actually, why do you know all about it?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.530
And the words you told Shu back then.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.410
Now, they remain only within me.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.210
The only thing I can do is apologize.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.970
Because I really am doing
something terrible.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:53.240
CRIME SYNDICATE
SERPIENTE
HEADQUARTERS

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.490
ODEN

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.870
So his memories...

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:58.490
Yep.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.500
You can only make one contract
if you use your soul...

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.250
but you can sell
your memories piece by piece.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:05.920
That idiot!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.380
So you believe me?

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.250
Shu has changed
ever since he partnered up with you!

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.920
It's as if he doesn't have
a future left anymore.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:18.350
Shu's still looking for the demon
that massacred his family to this day.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:22.100
And he's offering everything he has to do it.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.640
That's why he made a contract with me

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.230
to defeat Demonically Possessed
and gather information,

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:29.650
then look for a higher-ranking demon
with that information.

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.570
That's how he's chasing after the truth.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:33.860
I can't let him be reckless
like that anymore!

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:38.780
So that's why you didn't tell Shu anything
and tried to solve everything on your own, huh?

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.870
I don't know how you got
the police involved in all of this though.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.660
In the end, the police is nothing
more than a public office.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.380
They can't deny requests
from people in high places.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:51.880
So that auction cancellation the other day
was your doing, as well?

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:56.380
But in the end, I was saved by the one
I tried to interfere with. I'm so hopeless.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:00.390
Why do you go so far to rob
Shu's purpose in life? What's your plan?

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:04.390
It's so that he doesn't die, of course!

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:07.940
He's so reckless that he might die
each and every time!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:10.480
And he's losing his memories
on top of that!

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.650
At this rate, he'll stop
becoming himself at some point!

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.650
In the end, you'll eat every last bit of him!

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:19.410
But if he doesn't do that,
his wishes won't be granted.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:22.620
Avenging the enemy is fruitless
even if you were able to go through with it!

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.500
We'll see about that.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.250
It feels like Shu's seeking
something more than that.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.750
In the first place,
are you okay with him like that?

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:36.510
Are you happy being with someone basically
crippled for life with body and mind all torn up?

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.720
I don't mind.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:42.180
If I can be Shu's last girl.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:46.350
Looks like we'll never see eye to eye.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.270
Ever.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:52.690
Gotta hand it to the first girl
to look so unruffled.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.360
<i>We're speculating that</i>

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:04.370
<i>Orcas threw in another Demonically Possessed
to replace Tony Rossi from the other day,</i>

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.960
<i>and used that individual
to retaliate against Serpiente.</i>

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:09.290
Come on now.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:13.590
Don't bring demons into conflict
between mafia groups. Gimme a break!

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:17.380
<i>A police force is currently
surrounding the Orcas hideout.</i>

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:23.050
<i>But with the possibility that a Demonically Possessed
may be lurking inside, they're still on standby.</i>

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:27.600
So that's why you want a Demon Hazard
authorization right now?

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:33.770
<i>The chief of Metropolitan Police has also made
a strong request for emergency countermeasures.</i>

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:38.780
Jeez! The little chief can tell us directly
if he's in such a rush!

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:41.240
He has a clear line
between work and private life.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.490
A lot more than I can say for you.

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:45.780
Is he really that type though?

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:49.660
What just happened?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.830
Please give us orders to rush in!

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.920
No, we don't have a weapon that can
stand up against a Demonically Possessed—

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.210
Out! Out of the way!

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:07.640
That just now...

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:10.890
Shu! He's being reckless again!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.790
Hey, you're...

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.370
I see.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.710
You arbitrarily decide and execute
a lot more than I ever expected.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:22.090
It's true that we're powerless
against Demonically Possessed.

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:25.680
Though, I believe we can
at least act as your backup.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.430
What's the meaning of this,
Assistant Inspector?

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:31.680
Wasn't the Demonically Possessed
someone from Orcas?

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:35.310
Ma... ria...

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:37.940
Hey!

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.860
Did he just say "Maria"?

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:42.820
Maria... That girl dating Tony?

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:44.700
My goodness!

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:50.080
If this is her doing, then every premise
we've gone on loses meaning!

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.290
Wh-What do you mean by that?

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:56.460
This massacre isn't
one mafia retaliation after another!

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:59.710
It may simply be personal revenge!

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:05.840
She may be planning to murder everyone
involved in roping her loved one into a war...

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:09.800
and leaving him to die so easily, perhaps?

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:20.480
Jeez, you still have something—

00:23:55.580 --> 00:24:00.000
EPISODE 5
FLEETING SCARS

00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:58.950
"Fleeting Scars."
